    <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">
      Source L/h values are canonical. US GPM is derived as L/h &divide; 227.124707 and rounded to two decimals. HFO values above apply only to WHPX 407; none is transferred to MOPX 207. See the <a href="/technical-data/">technical-data methodology</a> and <a href="/technical-data/dolphin-dmpx-028.json">machine-readable DMPX-028 record</a>.
    </p>

    <InstallationRequirements />

    <!-- Key Applications -->
    <h2 id="key-applications">Key Applications</h2>

    <h3>Waste Oil Reclamation</h3>
    <p>
      The DMPX-028 can process industrial used-oil streams including used motor oil, hydraulic oil, and gear oil, separating water and particulate solids. Waste-oil throughput is application-specific and must be sized from viscosity, temperature, density difference, solids loading, and the selected base machine. See our <a href="/waste-oil-centrifuge/">waste oil centrifuge</a> application page for details.
    </p>

    <h3>Biodiesel Production</h3>
    <p>
      The DMPX-028 is used in <a href="/biodiesel-centrifuge/">biodiesel</a> finishing to remove residual methanol, water, and glycerin after transesterification. The published diesel values are not biodiesel ratings; Dolphin sizes this duty from the actual feed and separation target.
    </p>

    <h3>HFO Purification</h3>
    <p>
      On the WHPX 407 base machine, published <a href="/fuel-oil-centrifuge/">HFO</a> 380 cSt capacity is 2,300 L/h (10.13 US GPM derived), with viscosity specified at 50&deg;C and centrifugation at 98&deg;C. The HFO curve belongs only to WHPX 407 and is not a MOPX 207 rating.
    </p>

    <h3>Hydraulic &amp; Lube Oil Maintenance</h3>
    <p>
      Published <a href="/lube-oil-centrifuge/">lube-oil</a> capacity is 2,600 L/h (11.45 US GPM derived) for MOPX 207 R&amp;O / engine lube oil and 2,700&ndash;3,200 L/h (11.89&ndash;14.09 US GPM derived) for WHPX 407 cross-head R&amp;O oil, both centrifuged at 80&ndash;90&deg;C. Other lube-oil duties require application sizing.
    </p>

    <h3>Machining Coolant &amp; Quench Oil</h3>
    <p>
      The DMPX-028 platform also handles <a href="/machine-coolant-centrifuge/">machining coolant</a> separation, <a href="/quench-oil-centrifuge/">quench oil</a> clarification, and <a href="/cutting-oil-centrifuge/">cutting oil</a> recovery in metalworking operations - applications listed for both the Alfa Laval MOPX 207 and WHPX 407 base machines.
    </p>

    <!-- Mid-Page CTA -->
